+      "what_changes": "Create one immutable calibration record for each state before any paired measurement. Store `state_id`, task and episode identifiers, the starting observation and preprocessing record, simulator snapshot, controller state, ordered history, all random-number-generator streams, cache state, model/checkpoint identity, site-registry revision, and environment identity. Serialize one common baseline snapshot, then clone it into the FP16 reference branch and each candidate branch; restore each branch in a fixed order: model/checkpoint state, simulator state, controller state, history buffers, RNG streams, and cache contents plus keys and eviction metadata. The controller record must include policy hidden state, timestep, queued action chunk, and mode; the history record must preserve ordered observations, actions, rewards, and termination flags; the cache record must preserve scope and invalidation state. After restoration, replay the same baseline input and require the reference branch to reproduce the recorded observation and action output before measuring a site. The manifest must contain the exact Fast-WAM checkpoint identity and, when the Optional `idm` path is used, the exact Optional `idm` checkpoint identity and configuration. 【author decision: supply the immutable checkpoint identities and the exact-match fields for Fast-WAM and Optional `idm`; missing or mismatched identity must halt with no fallback artifact.】 The environment record must include CPU thread/process limits and the accelerator model and visible-memory class, explicitly distinguishing an 80GB-class run from an A100-40GB run. 【author decision: fix those execution-environment fields and the 80GB-class versus A100-40GB boundary in the manifest, including the memory-allocation policy.】 If any required identity or restoration check fails, halt before paired branch creation.",
+      "what_to_do_en": "Create one immutable calibration record for each state before any paired measurement. Store the state identifier, task and episode identifiers, starting observation and preprocessing record, simulator snapshot, controller state, ordered history, all random-number-generator (RNG) streams, cache state, model/checkpoint identity, site-registry revision, and environment identity. Serialize one common baseline snapshot, then clone it into the 16-bit floating-point (FP16) reference branch and one candidate branch per site; restore each branch in a fixed order: model/checkpoint state, simulator state, controller state, history buffers, RNG streams, and cache contents with keys and invalidation metadata. The controller record must include policy hidden state, timestep, queued action chunk, and mode; the history record must preserve ordered observations, actions, rewards, and termination flags; the cache record must preserve scope and invalidation state. After restoration, replay the same baseline input and require the reference branch to reproduce the recorded observation and action output before measuring a site. Store the exact Fast-WAM checkpoint identity and, when Optional `idm` is used, the exact Optional `idm` checkpoint identity and configuration in the manifest. 【author decision: supply the immutable Fast-WAM and Optional `idm` checkpoint identities and exact-match fields; a missing or mismatched identity must halt with no fallback artifact.】 Store the central processing unit (CPU) thread/process limits and accelerator model and visible-memory class as environment fields, explicitly distinguishing an 80GB-class run from an A100-40GB run. 【author decision: fix those environment fields and the 80GB-class versus A100-40GB boundary in the manifest, including the memory-allocation policy.】 If any required identity or restoration check fails, halt before creating paired branches.",
+      "what_to_do_zh": "在任何 paired measurement 之前，为每个 state 建立一条不可变的 calibration record。 记录 `state_id`、task 与 episode identifiers、starting observation 与 preprocessing record、simulator snapshot、controller state、ordered history、所有随机数生成器(Random Number Generator, RNG) state、cache state、model/checkpoint identity、site-registry revision 和 environment identity。 序列化一份共同 baseline，再从它 clone 出 16-bit floating-point (FP16) reference branch 和每个 site 的 candidate branch；按固定顺序恢复 model/checkpoint state、simulator state、controller state、history buffers、RNG streams，以及带有 keys 和 invalidation metadata 的 cache contents。 controller record 必须包括 policy hidden state、timestep、queued action chunk 和 mode；history record 必须保留按顺序排列的 observations、actions、rewards 与 termination flags；cache record 必须保留 scope 与 invalidation state。 恢复后 replay 同一个 baseline input，并要求 reference branch 在测量 site 之前重现已记录的 observation 和 action output。 manifest 必须保存 exact Fast-WAM checkpoint identity；如果使用 Optional `idm`，还必须保存 exact Optional `idm` checkpoint identity 与 configuration。 【作者需决定：提供 Fast-WAM 与 Optional `idm` 的不可变 checkpoint identities 及 exact-match fields；identity 缺失或不匹配时必须 halt，且不得 fallback 到其他 artifact。】 environment record 必须保存 central processing unit (CPU) 的 thread/process limits、accelerator model 与 visible-memory class，并明确区分 80GB-class 与 A100-40GB run。 【作者需决定：在 manifest 中固定这些 environment fields 以及 80GB-class 与 A100-40GB 的边界，并写明 memory-allocation policy。】 任何必需 identity 或 restoration check 失败，都必须在建立 paired branches 之前 halt。"
+    },
+    {
+      "step_id": "S2",
+      "what_changes": "Build a versioned site registry with stable `site_id`, module path or graph edge, tensor role (weight or activation), shape, dtype, capture point, and quantization granularity. For each candidate record, restore the S1 baseline, apply a mask containing exactly one `site_id`, quantize the selected weight tensor or intercept the selected activation at its registered graph edge, and leave every other target site at FP16. Record the operator parameters and verify that the mask changed only the selected site. The low-bit operator must be declared as either fake quantization or a real low-bit execution kernel, and the declared path must be used unchanged in calibration and held-out evaluation. 【author decision: choose and register `b_lo`, signedness, rounding, clipping, scale/zero-point, granularity, activation calibration data, and fake-quantization versus real-kernel mode; record backend/version and runtime verification when a real kernel is claimed.】 This is a single-site FP16-background intervention, not a joint-low-bit marginal or a joint-optimal schedule; QuantWM and QuantWAMs remain boundaries for their broader quantization scopes.",
+      "what_to_do_en": "Build a versioned site registry for weight/activation (W/A) sites with a stable `site_id`, module path or graph edge, tensor shape, data type, capture point, and quantization granularity. For each candidate, restore the S1 baseline, apply a mask containing exactly one `site_id`, quantize the selected weight tensor or intercept the selected activation at its registered graph edge, and leave every other target site at 16-bit floating-point (FP16). Record the operator parameters and verify that the mask changed only the selected site. Declare the low-bit operator as either fake quantization or a real low-bit execution kernel, and use that declared path unchanged in calibration and held-out evaluation. 【author decision: choose and register `b_lo`, signedness, rounding, clipping, scale/zero-point, granularity, activation calibration data, and fake-quantization versus real-kernel mode; record backend/version and runtime verification when a real kernel is claimed.】 This is a single-site FP16-background intervention, not a joint-low-bit marginal or joint-optimal schedule; QuantWM and QuantWAMs remain prior-art boundaries for their broader quantization scopes.",
+      "what_to_do_zh": "建立一个 versioned site registry，给 weight/activation (W/A) site 配置稳定的 `site_id`、module path 或 graph edge、tensor shape、dtype、capture point 与 quantization granularity。 对每个 candidate，先恢复 S1 baseline，再应用只包含一个 `site_id` 的 mask；在注册的 graph edge 上量化选定的 weight tensor 或截取选定的 activation，其余 target sites 全部保持 16-bit floating-point (FP16)。 记录 operator parameters，并验证 mask 只改变了被选中的 site。 必须把 low-bit operator 声明为 fake quantization（图级仿真）或真实的 low-bit execution kernel，并在 calibration 与 held-out evaluation 中保持同一条已声明路径。 【作者需决定：选择并登记 `b_lo`、signedness、rounding、clipping、scale/zero-point、granularity、activation calibration data，以及 fake-quantization 与 real-kernel mode；若声称使用真实 kernel，还要记录 backend/version 并做 runtime verification。】 这只是 single-site、FP16-background 的 intervention，不是 joint-low-bit marginal 或 joint-optimal schedule；QuantWM 与 QuantWAMs 的更广 quantization scope 仍属于 prior-art boundary。"
+    },
+    {
+      "step_id": "S3",
+      "what_changes": "From each restored reference/candidate pair, run inference once and capture the complete action chunk before executing any action. Preserve its time dimension, action-component order, valid-length mask, and dtype, and store the exact chunk for each branch. Restore the same baseline independently for each branch, execute only the first action, and capture the immediate next observation plus terminal, simulator-error, and preprocessing-status flags. Write one row per (`state_id`, `site_id`, branch) with both chunks, both next observations, the two component discrepancies, and the local discrepancy. Use the normalized full-action-chunk MSE term and next-observation pixel L1 term to form `C_r`. 【author decision: define the denominators, valid-element masks, observation preprocessing, and fixed scale or relative weighting that make the two terms commensurate; the sum notation does not supply these choices.】 Aggregate state rows into the sitewise value used for ranking and state-subset correlation. 【author decision: choose the aggregation order and statistic, state pooling rule, and missing-state handling for the sitewise `C_r`.】 Compute the local discrepancy from an explicitly registered weight or activation tensor comparison using the same calibration rows. 【author decision: define the local-score tensor pair, sample set, normalization, and sitewise aggregation; do not substitute `C_r` for the local score.】 Apply one identical inclusion policy to terminal, invalid, simulator-error, missing-observation, and variable-length rows. 【author decision: specify whether each such row is retained, masked, or excluded and how the reason is recorded.】 `C_r` is only the paired one-control-transition proxy: it contains no task-loss term, no post-first-action rollout or replan marginal, and no jointly-low-bit background.",
+      "what_to_do_en": "Run the reference and one-site branch from matched restored states. Save each complete action chunk before any action is executed, including its time length, action ordering, valid-step mask, and data type. Restore the state separately for each branch, execute only the first action, and save the immediate next observation and terminal or simulator-error flags. Store one row per state and site with both chunks, both observations, the two component differences, and the local difference. Use the mean-squared error (MSE) of the full action chunks and the next-observation pixel L1 difference to form `C_r`. 【author decision: define the denominators, valid-element masks, observation preprocessing, and fixed scale or relative weighting that put the two terms on a common scale; the sum notation does not decide this.】 Combine state rows into the site-level value used for ranking and state-subset rank correlation. 【author decision: choose the aggregation order and statistic, state pooling rule, and missing-state handling for the site-level `C_r`.】 Calculate the local discrepancy from a declared weight or activation tensor comparison using the same calibration rows. 【author decision: define the local-score tensor pair, sample set, normalization, and site-level aggregation; do not use `C_r` as a substitute for the local score.】 Choose one inclusion policy for terminal, invalid, simulator-error, missing-observation, and variable-length rows and apply it to both branches. 【author decision: specify whether each such row is retained, masked, or excluded and how its reason is recorded.】 `C_r` is only a one-control-transition proxy: it is not task loss, a rollout or replan marginal after the first action, or a jointly-low-bit result.",
+      "what_to_do_zh": "让 reference branch 与 single-site branch 从匹配的 restored states 分别运行一次推理。 在执行任何 action 之前保存完整 action chunk，并保留其 time length、action ordering、valid-step mask 与 dtype。 为每个 branch 分别恢复同一个 state，只执行第一个 action，然后保存 immediate next observation 以及 terminal 或 simulator-error flags。 每个 state 和 site 写入一行记录，包含两个 branch 的 action chunks、observations、两项 component differences 与 local difference。 用完整 action chunks 的均方误差(mean squared error, MSE)和 next-observation 的 pixel L1 difference 构成 `C_r`。 【作者需决定：定义 action-chunk term 与 image term 的 denominators、valid-element masks、observation preprocessing，以及让两项处于可比较尺度的固定 scale 或 relative weighting；sum notation 本身不提供这些选择。】 把 state rows 聚合成用于 ranking 和 state-subset rank correlation 的 site-level value。 【作者需决定：确定聚合顺序与 statistic、state pooling rule，以及 site-level `C_r` 的 missing-state handling。】 使用同一批 calibration rows，从明确登记的 weight 或 activation tensor comparison 计算 local discrepancy。 【作者需决定：定义 local-score tensor pair、sample set、normalization 与 site-level aggregation；不能用 `C_r` 替代 local score。】 为 terminal、invalid、simulator-error、missing-observation 与 variable-length rows 选择一套 inclusion policy，并对两个 branch 一致执行。 【作者需决定：说明每类 row 是 retained、masked 还是 excluded，以及如何记录对应 reason。】 `C_r` 只表示 paired one-control-transition proxy：它不包含 task loss、首个 action 之后的 rollout 或 replan marginal，也不包含 jointly-low-bit background。"
+    },
+    {
+      "step_id": "S4",
+      "what_changes": "Construct two deterministic protection schedules from the same site registry: one sorted by `C_r` and one by local discrepancy. Sort descending and break ties by stable lexical `site_id`; select the protected set using the same high-precision-unit allowance `B` and declared site count `B_site`, keep protected sites at FP16, and keep unprotected target sites at the declared `b_lo`. 【author decision: supply numeric `B` and `B_site`, define what one high-precision unit represents for each W/A site, and state whether both are hard constraints or how conflicts are resolved.】 Store each schedule with site IDs, W/A role, tensor shape, dtype, precision, and the exact selected-unit count. Site count is only a count of site IDs; it is not packed bytes or latency. 【author decision: decide whether any real-bytes or latency result is in scope; if yes, add a separate packing and timing protocol covering dtype packing, kernel/backend, warm-up, synchronization, and aggregation, and otherwise label those outcomes out of scope.】 Apply the two schedules with identical branch restoration, input order, and evaluation manifest so only the ranking source differs.",
+      "what_to_do_en": "Construct two deterministic protection schedules from the same site registry: one sorted by `C_r` and one sorted by the local discrepancy. For weight/activation (W/A) sites, sort each list from largest score to smallest and break ties by stable lexical `site_id`; select the protected set using the same high-precision-unit allowance `B` and declared site count `B_site`, keep protected sites at 16-bit floating-point (FP16), and keep unprotected target sites at the declared `b_lo`. 【author decision: provide numeric `B` and `B_site`, define what one high-precision unit represents for each W/A site, and state whether both are hard constraints or how conflicts are resolved.】 Store each schedule with site identifiers, W/A role, tensor shape, data type, precision, and the exact selected-unit count. A site count is only a count of site identifiers; it is not packed bytes or latency. 【author decision: decide whether any real-bytes or latency result is in scope; if yes, add a separate packing and timing protocol covering data-type packing, kernel/backend, warm-up, synchronization, and aggregation; otherwise label those outcomes out of scope.】 Apply both schedules with identical branch restoration, input order, and evaluation manifest so only the ranking source differs.",
+      "what_to_do_zh": "使用同一个 site registry 建立两份 deterministic protection schedule：一份按 `C_r` 排序，另一份按 local discrepancy 排序。 对 weight/activation (W/A) sites 按 score 从大到小排序，并用稳定的字典序 `site_id` 处理 ties；在相同的 high-precision-unit allowance `B` 与声明的 site count `B_site` 下选择 protected set，把 protected sites 保持为 16-bit floating-point (FP16)，把未保护的 target sites 保持为声明的 `b_lo`。 【作者需决定：提供数值化的 `B` 与 `B_site`，定义每个 W/A site 的一个 high-precision unit 代表什么，并说明两者是否都是 hard constraints，或冲突时如何处理。】 为每份 schedule 保存 site identifiers、W/A role、tensor shape、dtype、precision 与 exact selected-unit count。 site count 只表示 site identifiers 的数量，不等于 packed bytes 或 latency。 【作者需决定：说明是否要报告 real-bytes 或 latency；若要报告，必须另加 packing 与 timing protocol，涵盖 dtype packing、kernel/backend、warm-up、synchronization 与 aggregation；否则明确把这些 outcome 标为 out of scope。】 对两份 schedule 使用完全相同的 branch restoration、input order 与 evaluation manifest，使唯一差异来自 ranking source。"
+    },
+    {
+      "step_id": "S5",
+      "what_changes": "Use the immutable S1 manifest to run `idm` with `sigma_shift_FW=1.0` and `infer_action` on the named held-out RoboTwin 2.0/LIBERO manipulation split. Hold the declared `b_lo`, `B`, `B_site`, preprocessing, reset protocol, controller restoration, and branch order fixed across the two schedules. Enumerate the held-out task IDs, episode and initial-state IDs, seeds, split membership, contact-transition predicate from simulator events, and task success/failure rule before inspecting results. 【author decision: supply the exact split and contact/failure definitions, including whether a contact transition is required before the first action or may occur after it.】 For each paired episode, restore the same initial state for both schedules, run the declared evaluation horizon, and record task outcome and the next-observation deviation with its aggregation window. 【author decision: pin the `idm` and `infer_action` entrypoint revisions and arguments, action horizon, termination rule, and whether next-observation deviation is first-transition-only or later-transition/full-episode; keep any latter summary separate from `C_r`.】 Build the permutation control by reassigning the recorded `C_r` values across the same site IDs while preserving the score multiset, `B`, `B_site`, tie-breaking, and all other schedule rules. Use the specified oracle simulator-state branch only as a labeled positive control. 【author decision: specify the permutation seed and replicate/list, the oracle state source, the branch insertion point, and the comparison it controls; do not use it as a substitute for the real association.】 Interpret the result narrowly: `C_r` remains a one-control-transition ranking proxy, while task failures and any full-horizon summaries are separate downstream outcomes rather than task loss or a full-horizon/replan marginal. QuantWM and QuantWAMs retain their broader WAM quantization boundaries; VAML, Model Advantage / Value-Aware Model Learning, Deep Task-Based Quantization, and SQIL retain prior-art ownership of broad consequence-, value-, task-, or critical-state-protection principles.",
+      "what_to_do_en": "Use the immutable S1 manifest to run the `idm` entrypoint with `sigma_shift_FW=1.0` and `infer_action` on the named held-out RoboTwin 2.0/LIBERO manipulation split. Use the same declared `b_lo`, `B`, `B_site`, preprocessing, reset procedure, controller restoration, and branch order for the two schedules. List the held-out task identifiers, episode and initial-state identifiers, seeds, split membership, simulator-event contact predicate, and task success/failure rule before inspecting results. 【author decision: provide the exact split and contact/failure definitions, including whether contact must occur before the first action or may occur after it.】 For each paired episode, restore the same initial state for both schedules, run the declared evaluation horizon, and record task outcome and next-observation deviation with its aggregation window. 【author decision: pin the `idm` and `infer_action` entrypoint revisions and arguments, action horizon, termination rule, and whether next-observation deviation is first-transition-only or later-transition/full-episode; keep any later summary separate from `C_r`.】 Create the permutation control by reassigning the recorded `C_r` values across the same site identifiers while preserving the score multiset, `B`, `B_site`, tie-breaking, and every other schedule rule. Run the specified oracle simulator-state branch only as a labeled positive-control branch. 【author decision: specify the permutation seed and replicate/list, oracle state source, branch insertion point, and controlled comparison; do not use the oracle as a substitute for the real association.】 Keep the interpretation bounded: `C_r` is a one-control-transition ranking proxy, while task failures and full-horizon summaries are separate downstream outcomes, not task loss or a full-horizon/replan marginal. QuantWM and QuantWAMs retain their broader world action model (WAM) quantization boundaries; VAML, Model Advantage / Value-Aware Model Learning, Deep Task-Based Quantization, and SQIL retain prior-art ownership of broad consequence-, value-, task-, or critical-state-protection principles.",
+      "what_to_do_zh": "使用不可变的 S1 manifest，在命名的 held-out RoboTwin 2.0/LIBERO manipulation split 上运行带有 `sigma_shift_FW=1.0` 的 `idm` entrypoint 与 `infer_action`。 对两份 schedule 使用相同的声明性 `b_lo`、`B`、`B_site`、preprocessing、reset procedure、controller restoration 与 branch order。 在查看结果之前，列出 held-out task identifiers、episode 与 initial-state identifiers、seeds、split membership、来自 simulator events 的 contact predicate，以及 task success/failure rule。 【作者需决定：提供 exact split 与 contact/failure definitions，包括 contact 是否必须在第一个 action 之前发生，还是允许在之后发生。】 对每个 paired episode，为两份 schedule 恢复同一个 initial state，运行声明的 evaluation horizon，并记录 task outcome 与带有 aggregation window 的 next-observation deviation。 【作者需决定：固定 `idm` 与 `infer_action` entrypoint revisions 和 arguments、action horizon、termination rule，并决定 next-observation deviation 只看 first transition，还是覆盖 later transition/full episode；后者必须与 `C_r` 分开汇总。】 建立 permutation control：在相同 site identifiers 之间重新分配已记录的 `C_r` values，同时保持 score multiset、`B`、`B_site`、tie-breaking 与其他 schedule rules 不变。 指定的 oracle simulator-state branch 只能作为标注清楚的 positive-control branch 运行。 【作者需决定：指定 permutation seed 与 replicate/list、oracle state source、branch insertion point 以及它所控制的 comparison；不能用 oracle 替代真实 association。】 保持解释边界：`C_r` 仍是 one-control-transition ranking proxy；task failures 与 full-horizon summaries 是独立的 downstream outcomes，不是 task loss，也不是 full-horizon/replan marginal。 QuantWM 与 QuantWAMs 继续保留其更广的 world action model (WAM) quantization boundaries；VAML、Model Advantage / Value-Aware Model Learning、Deep Task-Based Quantization 与 SQIL 继续代表 broad consequence、value-aware、task-based 或 critical-state-protection principles 的 prior-art boundary。"
+    }
+  ]
+}

