+      "fill": "Authors must provide numeric `B` and `B_site`, define what one high-precision unit represents for each W/A site, state whether both are hard constraints or how conflicts are resolved, and specify the selection rule when they conflict; do not silently replace one with the other.",
+      "severity": "open"
+    },
+    {
+      "step_id": "S4",
+      "hole": "A site-count schedule has no mapping to packed bytes or measured latency, although sites may have different shapes and execution paths.",
+      "fill": "Authors must decide whether any real-bytes or latency result is in scope; if yes, add a separate packing and timing protocol covering dtype packing, kernel/backend, warm-up, synchronization, and aggregation, and otherwise label those outcomes out of scope. Site count alone must never be reported as real bytes or latency.",
+      "severity": "open"
+    },
+    {
+      "step_id": "S5",
+      "hole": "The held-out RoboTwin 2.0/LIBERO split and contact-sensitive subset are named but not enumerated or labeled.",
+      "fill": "Authors must list exact task and episode IDs, initial-state IDs, seeds, split membership, and the contact-transition predicate from logged simulator events; define task failure and success aggregation before inspecting results.",
+      "severity": "open"
+    },
+    {
+      "step_id": "S5",
+      "hole": "The exact `idm`/`infer_action` invocation and next-observation comparison window are not defined.",
+      "fill": "Authors must pin the entrypoint revision, model/config arguments, preprocessing, action horizon, reset protocol, termination rule, and whether next-observation deviation is measured only at the first post-action transition or over later transitions; keep the latter separate from `C_r`.",
+      "severity": "open"
+    },
+    {
